<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Süleymaniye Mosque</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Süleymaniye Mosque is an imperial mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> built for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> by the architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mimar-sinan">Mimar Sinan</a> in the 1550s. It is one of the largest and most celebrated works of Ottoman architecture. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> cite it as a high point of Sinan's architectural programme.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suleymaniye-mosque.jpg" alt="Süleymaniye Mosque" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hunanuk · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%BCleymaniyeMosqueIstanbul_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
